8.5  Phase 4: Balance Critic

The Balance Critic identifies three issues. First, a runaway leader problem in cooperative play: if one player’s strain grows faster, they dominate decisions (severity: moderate; recommendation: add a network synergy rule so connected strains share benefits). Second, arbitrary flood timing: random event cards determining flood speed leaves players with no agency over the core tension (severity: moderate; recommendation: make flood a predictable escalation of one level per round, with events as modifiers). Third, engine building as a potential trap: structures costing growth may cause builders to fall behind (severity: minor; recommendation: structures should provide an immediate small benefit plus an ongoing ability).
8.6  Phase 5: Refinement

The refinement agent addresses both moderate-severity issues: it adds a Network Synergy rule (adjacent strains share engine abilities), changes flood timing to a predictable one-level-per-round baseline with event modifiers, and rebalances structures to provide an immediate 1 VP plus their ongoing ability.
8.7  Phase 6: Fun Factor Judge

The Fun Factor Judge rates the refined design 7/10. Engagement hooks include persistent tension (“Will we reach the surface in time?”), simultaneous placement creating reveal anticipation, and structure building as achievement. Tension moments include the visible flood countdown, event card reveals, and decisions about saving endangered colonies versus abandoning them. Replayability stems from modular board setup, different strain combinations (4!=24 team configurations), and event deck variability.
